":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nPresent in v4.7.rc2.official [3df26a02c] as well as RC1\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.rc2 - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4060 Ti (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.7700) - AMD Ryzen 5 3600X 6-Core Processor (12 threads) - 31.93 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Surround 7.1)\n\n### Issue description\n\nRelevant to: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119692\nModifying the scale of a CanvasItem to which another CanvasItem is a child will not cause the children to be resampled.\nUpdating the child transform afterward (even by setting the position to the same value) will cause the resample.\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create a 2D/Control scene\n2. Add a child node using DPITexture\n3. Disable \"Auto resample CanvasItems\" in the editor viewport's View menu to replicate usual in-game conditions\n4. Adjust scale of parent node\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[4.7-rc2-resampling.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/28871863/4.7-rc2-resampling.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120235/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120235/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}